---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_GITHUB_URL } from '../constants';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - Kery"
  description="Privacy policy for kery.dev and Kery open-source and future hosted services."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="container legal-inner">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: April 4, 2026</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        “Kery” refers to the open-source software project and this website (<strong>kery.dev</strong>). This policy
        describes how we handle information in connection with the marketing site and how we expect deployments
        of the software to behave by default.
      </p>

      <h2>2. This website (kery.dev)</h2>
      <p>
        The static marketing site is designed not to require accounts. We do not intentionally collect personal
        data through forms on this site. Our hosting provider may process standard server or edge logs (such as IP
        address, user agent, and request path) for security and reliability - refer to your host’s documentation
        for retention and subprocessors.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we add analytics, newsletters, or account-based features later, we will update this policy and, where
        required, provide appropriate notice and choices.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Self-hosted Kery (open source)</h2>
      <p>
        When you run Kery yourself, you control the infrastructure. Test artifacts, credentials, LLM prompts,
        database contents, and logs reside in <strong>your</strong> environment. The open-source project does not
        phone home by default; review the repository and your configuration for any optional integrations you enable.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Future hosted Kery (“Kery Cloud”)</h2>
      <p>
        A managed offering may collect and process personal data to operate the service - for example account
        details, billing, support correspondence, and operational telemetry needed to run the product. We will
        publish a dedicated privacy notice and data processing terms before any hosted service accepts customers.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        Kery can be configured to call third-party AI providers (for example language model APIs). Those calls are
        governed by your agreements with those vendors. You are responsible for the categories of data you send to
        them and for complying with applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict certain personal
        data. For data processed only on your self-hosted deployment, exercise those rights with your own
        organization. For data we process as a controller through this site or a future hosted product, contact us
        using the channels listed on <a href={SITE_GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a> once published.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the product and site evolve. Material changes will be reflected by updating the
        date above and, where appropriate, an announcement in the repository or on this site.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be opened as a discussion or issue on the
        <a href={SITE_GITHUB_URL}>Kery GitHub repository</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding-top: 6rem;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    min-height: 60vh;
  }

  .legal-inner {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal-inner h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .legal-inner h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-inner p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-inner a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .legal-inner a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
  }
</style>
